Here are several description options depending on how you want to position **Uriel Studio**.

### Recommended (VS Marketplace)

```text
A professional writing environment for authors, worldbuilders, and storytellers. Organize manuscripts, characters, lore, timelines, prophecies, and AI-assisted writing in one integrated VS Code extension.
```

---

### Short Description (package.json)

```text
A professional writing environment for authors and worldbuilders.
```

---

### Feature-Oriented Description

```text
Uriel Studio transforms Visual Studio Code into a complete writing workspace for novels, series, and fictional universes. Manage manuscripts, chapters, scenes, characters, locations, artifacts, timelines, prophecies, and interconnected lore with built-in templates, snippets, project generation, and publishing tools.
```

---

### Marketplace Description

```text
Uriel Studio is an authoring environment built for long-form storytelling.

Features include:

• Project generation
• Manuscript organization
• Character and worldbuilding templates
• Lore and codex management
• Timeline planning
• Relationship mapping
• AI writing workflows
• Custom snippets
• Markdown authoring
• Publishing tools
• Export support
• Integrated writing dashboard

Whether you're writing a standalone novel or a multi-book series, Uriel Studio helps keep your story organized, searchable, and consistent.
```

---

### Vision Statement

```text
Uriel Studio is a specialized IDE for fiction writing, combining manuscript management, knowledge organization, and authoring tools into a single workspace. Built on Visual Studio Code, it provides a structured environment for creating complex stories while maintaining consistency across characters, settings, timelines, and lore.
```

## Recommended `package.json`

```json
{
  "name": "uriel-studio",
  "displayName": "Uriel Studio",
  "description": "A professional writing environment for authors, worldbuilders, and storytellers. Organize manuscripts, characters, lore, timelines, and AI-assisted writing in one integrated VS Code extension."
}
```

This description accurately reflects the project's goals without promising features that aren't yet implemented, while leaving room for future expansion.
